course: dictionary
lesson: 12299
title: Coordinated: moving and working together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Coordinated» describes things that work together smoothly. A coordinated person moves their hands, feet and eyes together well. A coordinated plan is organised so that everyone knows their job. The word has more than one meaning, so use the other words in the sentence to choose the right one.
explain: «Mia's coordinated catch was perfect: her eyes tracked the ball and her hands closed around it at just the right moment.» The clues are catch and ball, so this is about moving the body well. «The school trip was well coordinated, and every teacher knew when and where to meet.» Here the clues are trip and teachers: the plan ran smoothly.
explain: Coordinated can also describe clothes that match. «Her coordinated outfit had a green top, green socks and a green bow.» Ask yourself what word would fit here. Then swap in your meaning, such as matching or organised, and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Coordinated means able to move different parts of your body together well and smoothly.
fact: Coordinated also means organised so that people or things work well together.
fact: A coordinated outfit has clothes and colours that match.
fact: Coordinate is the verb: «The captain coordinates the team» means the captain organises the team so they work together.
fact: In maths, coordinates are the numbers that show a point on a grid. It is a related word, but it is used in a different way.
exercise: «The dancers were coordinated, and every step landed on the beat.» What does coordinated mean here? | Very loud and noisy | Covered in paint | *Moving together well and smoothly | Lost and confused
exercise: «Sam's team had a coordinated plan, so everyone knew their job.» What does coordinated mean here? | *Organised so people work well together | Written in red ink | Broken and forgotten
exercise: «Her coordinated scarf and hat were both bright blue.» What does coordinated suggest? | *Matching | Too big for her | Dirty and torn | Lost somewhere in the house
test: «The goalkeeper's coordinated dive stopped the ball.» Which word is closest in meaning to coordinated here? | Slow | Clumsy | Careless | *Smooth
test: Which word could replace coordinated in «a coordinated team» without changing the meaning? | *Organised | Tired | Noisy | Lonely
exam: «Pip's coordinated outfit matched the dance, and the plan was coordinated too.» Which two meanings does coordinated have in this sentence? | *Matching and organised | Old and broken | Wet and cold | Loud and fast
